 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "On his best colt, without delay,\nHe rode the road in the open air.\nWhen the cannon sounded forth again,\nIt was for a triumph of battle.\nAnd he had nothing to do again;\nHe was sleeping on himself.\nThus they sat and looked at himself,\nAs if the mysterious mysterious\nHad entered into their consciousness\nThrough a strange new channel within;\nThe same exact thought that enters us\nIn other men's minds alone.\nNevermore they walked through the forest,\nNor saw the garden beyond them,\nBut were instead by Apollo been,\nStruck with an irresistible dream,\nThat grew like a rising sun again,\nThat came with a sudden sudden\nChange of mood, or e'en as before,\nFrom the walking man again",
